    private fun story3() = EnStory(
        storyId = "adv_frankenstein",
        chapters = listOf(
            EnChapter(1, "The Young Scientist", listOf(
                "My name is Victor Frankenstein, and I was born in Geneva, Switzerland, into a family of wealth and distinction, a family that had long been respected in the city and that had always valued learning and honor above all other things.",
                "My father was a man of great wisdom and gentleness, and my mother was a woman of extraordinary kindness, and together they raised me with a love that I have never been able to forget, no matter how much suffering I have endured since their deaths.",
                "I had two brothers, Ernest and William, and though we were different in many ways, we loved each other dearly, and we spent our childhood in a state of happiness that I have never been able to recapture.",
                "I also had a dear friend named Henry Clerval, a young man of great imagination and goodness, who would remain my closest companion through all the trials that were to come.",
                "I was a curious child, and I loved to read and to learn, and I spent many hours poring over the ancient books of science and philosophy that I found in my father's library.",
                "I was particularly fascinated by the great questions of existence, by the mysteries of life and death, by the secrets that nature hides from ordinary men.",
                "One day, when I was about fifteen years old, I witnessed a terrible storm, and I saw lightning strike a great oak tree and shatter it into a thousand pieces.",
                "I was struck by the power of this natural force, and I began to wonder if there were other powers, hidden powers, that might be harnessed by men of science and daring.",
                "I decided that I would devote my life to the study of natural philosophy, and I resolved that I would one day make a discovery that would change the world.",
                "When I was seventeen, my mother died of scarlet fever, and her death devastated me, and it also deepened my obsession with the question of life and death.",
                "I began to wonder if death were truly the end, or if there were some way to conquer it, some way to bring the dead back to life, some way to defeat the greatest enemy of humanity.",
                "I went to the University of Ingolstadt, where I studied chemistry and natural philosophy under the greatest teachers of the age.",
                "One of my professors, Mr. Waldman, took an interest in me, and he taught me everything he knew about the secrets of the human body.",
                "I learned about the muscles and the nerves, about the circulation of the blood, about the mysterious force that animates the living flesh.",
                "And as I learned, I began to conceive of an idea, an idea so bold and so terrible that I did not dare to speak of it to anyone.",
                "I would create life from death, I would assemble a body from the parts of the dead, and I would give it the spark of existence.",
                "I would become a creator, a god, the first man to defeat death, the first man to bring the dead back to life.",
                "And so I began my great work, working day and night in a secret laboratory, gathering the materials that I would need.",
                "I visited graveyards and charnel houses, and I collected the parts that I required, and I began to assemble my creature piece by piece.",
                "The work was long and difficult, and it consumed me utterly, and I became pale and thin, and I lost touch with my family and my friends.",
                "But I could not stop, for I was too close to my goal, and the thought of what I might achieve drove me onward through every obstacle."
            )),
            EnChapter(2, "The Monster", listOf(
                "One night, in the darkness of November, I finally completed my work, and I gave life to the creature that I had assembled from the parts of the dead.",
                "The creature opened its eyes, and I saw that they were yellow and watery, and I saw that its skin was pale and stretched over its bones, and I saw that its lips were black and thin.",
                "It was hideous beyond description, a mockery of the human form, a thing that should never have been brought into existence.",
                "I had dreamed of creating beauty, of fashioning a new race of beings who would bless me as their creator, but instead I had created a monster, a thing of horror and disgust.",
                "I fled from the laboratory, and I wandered through the streets of Ingolstadt all night, unable to face what I had done.",
                "In the morning, I returned to my apartment, and I found that the creature was gone, and I was filled with relief and with terror in equal measure.",
                "I became ill with a fever that lasted for weeks, and I was nursed back to health by my faithful friend Henry Clerval, who had come to the university to study.",
                "When I finally recovered, I received a letter from my father, telling me that my younger brother William had been murdered.",
                "I rushed back to Geneva, and I learned that the killer had not been found, and that an innocent woman named Justine had been accused of the crime.",
                "I knew, in my heart, that Justine was innocent, and I suspected that the true killer was the creature that I had brought into the world.",
                "But I could not tell anyone, for who would believe me? Who would believe that I had created a living being from the parts of the dead?",
                "Justine was tried and convicted, and she was executed for a crime she did not commit, and I was consumed by guilt and by despair.",
                "Days later, I was walking in the mountains near Geneva, seeking solace in the beauty of nature, when I saw a figure approaching me through the mist.",
                "It was the creature, and when I saw it, I was filled with terror and hatred, and I demanded that it leave me alone.",
                "But the creature did not leave, and instead, it spoke to me in a voice that was soft and sad, and it told me that it wanted to tell me its story.",
                "I was astonished, for I had not imagined that the creature could speak, and I did not know what to do.",
                "But I was also curious, and I felt a strange sense of obligation to the being that I had created, and so I agreed to listen to what it had to say.",
                "And so the creature began to tell me the story of its life, a story of loneliness and rejection, a story that would break my heart and change everything."
            )),
            EnChapter(3, "The Creature's Story", listOf(
                "The creature told me that after leaving my apartment on the night of its creation, it had wandered through the countryside, frightened and alone, not knowing what it was or where it belonged.",
                "It had been driven away by every person it had encountered, for its appearance was so terrifying that no one could bear to look at it.",
                "It had found shelter in a small hut near a cottage, and it had watched the family that lived there, a poor but kind family named the De Laceys.",
                "Through watching them, the creature had learned to speak and to read, and it had come to understand the world in a way that it had not before.",
                "It had learned about love and kindness and family, and it had longed to be part of such a family itself.",
                "It had helped the De Laceys secretly, gathering firewood for them, and it had hoped that one day it might be accepted by them.",
                "But when it finally approached the blind father of the family, hoping that he might accept it despite its appearance, the other members of the family returned and drove it away in terror.",
                "The creature was heartbroken, and it began to hate the world that had rejected it, and it began to plot its revenge.",
                "It had found its way to Geneva, and there it had encountered my young brother William, and in a moment of rage, it had killed him.",
                "It had also arranged for the innocent Justine to be accused of the crime, so that others might share in its suffering.",
                "But even as it told me this, the creature wept, and it asked me why I had created it, why I had brought it into a world that would only hate and fear it.",
                "It told me that it was lonely beyond words, that it had never known a moment of kindness or love, and that it longed for a companion who would understand it.",
                "It asked me to create a female creature like itself, a mate who would share its life and its sorrow, and it promised that if I did so, it would leave the world of men forever.",
                "It promised to go with its companion to the wilds of South America, where no human being would ever see them, and to live out its days in peace.",
                "I was torn, for I could see the pain in the creature's eyes, and I felt a strange sense of responsibility for the suffering that I had caused.",
                "But I also feared what the creature might do if I gave it a companion, for two such beings might do even greater harm than one.",
                "I refused at first, but the creature pleaded with me, and finally, I agreed, for I could not bear to see it suffer any longer.",
                "I returned to my laboratory, and I began to work on the female creature, and for a time, I felt a strange sense of purpose.",
                "But as I worked, I began to imagine the terrible consequences of my actions, and I became convinced that I was doing something monstrous.",
                "I destroyed the female creature before I had finished it, and the creature, seeing this, was filled with rage and despair.",
                "It promised to take revenge on me, on my wedding night, and then it disappeared into the darkness, and I was left alone with my guilt and my fear."
            )),
            EnChapter(4, "The Revenge", listOf(
                "After the creature disappeared, I was consumed by a fear that would not leave me, for I knew that it would keep its promise to take revenge on my wedding night.",
                "I tried to prepare myself, but I did not know when or how the creature would strike, and the uncertainty was almost worse than the threat itself.",
                "In the months that followed, the creature struck again and again, always from the shadows, always in a way that I could not prevent.",
                "It killed my friend Henry Clerval, and it arranged for me to be accused of the murder, and I was imprisoned in Ireland for months before I was finally released.",
                "I returned to Geneva, and I married Elizabeth, my beloved childhood companion, hoping against hope that the creature's threat had been an empty one.",
                "But on the night of our wedding, while I was searching for the creature in the gardens, it stole into our room and strangled Elizabeth in her bed.",
                "I found her body in the morning, and I was destroyed by grief, for I had lost the last person I loved in the world.",
                "My father died a few days later, unable to bear the weight of his sorrow, and I was left alone with nothing but my hatred and my desire for revenge.",
                "I decided that I would hunt the creature down, that I would follow it to the ends of the earth, and that I would destroy it or die trying.",
                "And so I began my long pursuit, following the creature across Europe and Asia, always one step behind, always driven by my hatred and my grief.",
                "The creature left me clues, messages carved into trees and rocks, for it wanted me to keep chasing it, it wanted me to suffer as it had suffered.",
                "I followed it to the frozen north, to the icy wastes of the Arctic, where the cold was so intense that it seemed to burn the very air.",
                "My strength began to fail, and I became weak and ill, and I knew that I was dying, but still I could not give up.",
                "One day, I was rescued by a ship that was sailing to the North Pole, and I was taken aboard by a kind captain named Walton.",
                "I told him my story, the whole story, the story of my creation and my suffering, and he was horrified by what he heard.",
                "I became weaker by the day, and I knew that my death was near, but I was determined to tell my story to someone before I died.",
                "And then, one night, the creature came to my cabin, and it stood over me and looked at me with an expression that I could not read.",
                "It told me that it was sorry for what it had done, that it had never wanted to cause so much suffering, that it had only wanted to be loved.",
                "It told me that it had suffered more than any human being, that it had been rejected and hated from the moment of its creation, and that it had never known a single moment of kindness.",
                "It told me that it wanted to die, that it could not bear to live any longer, and that it would go to the far north and destroy itself in the flames.",
                "And then it left, and I was alone with my thoughts, and I knew that I had caused all of this, that everything that had happened was my fault, that I had destroyed everyone I loved.",
                "I died shortly after, alone, far from home, with nothing but my guilt and my sorrow to accompany me into the darkness."
            )),
            EnChapter(5, "The End of the Chase", listOf(
                "The captain buried me at sea, as I had requested, for I did not want my body to be found by anyone who might have known me.",
                "He wrote down my story, and he promised that he would send it to my family in Geneva, though I did not know if anyone was still alive to receive it.",
                "Some weeks after my death, the captain found the creature again, or rather the creature found the ship, and it climbed aboard and came to the captain's cabin.",
                "It stood before him and told him that it had kept its word, that it had gone to the far north and destroyed itself, and that it had come back to say goodbye.",
                "The captain was afraid, but he also felt a strange sense of pity for the creature, for he could see the terrible suffering in its eyes.",
                "The creature told the captain that it had never wanted to be evil, that it had only wanted to be loved, and that the world had made it into what it had become.",
                "It told him that my death had given it no pleasure, that it had only wanted me to understand what it had suffered, and that now that I was dead, it had nothing left to live for.",
                "It told him that it was sorry for what it had done, that it would spend eternity regretting the harm it had caused, and that it hoped one day to find peace.",
                "And then it left the ship, and it disappeared into the darkness of the frozen sea, and no one ever saw it again.",
                "Some say that it kept its promise, that it destroyed itself in the flames, and that it finally found the peace that had been denied it in life.",
                "Others say that it still walks the earth, alone and unloved, seeking the companionship that it could never find.",
                "I do not know which is true, and I suppose it does not matter, for the story of Frankenstein is not a story about a monster, but about a man.",
                "It is a story about a man who tried to play God, who tried to create life from death, and who learned that some things are not meant for human hands.",
                "It is a story about the dangers of knowledge without wisdom, of power without responsibility, of ambition without compassion.",
                "It is a story about the consequences of our actions, and about the responsibility that we bear for the things that we create.",
                "It is a story about loneliness and rejection, about the human need for love and acceptance, about the terrible things that can happen when that need is denied.",
                "And it is a story that will be told and retold for generations to come, for its lessons are as relevant today as they were when I first wrote them down."
            ))
        )
    )
